# Keep everything under .lokf/ on LF, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf
# says. Git for Windows defaults to CRLF checkouts, and the conventions
# script, the Obsidian plugins and the toolkit must read the same bytes on
# every machine - a Windows checkout used to disagree with CI over the same
# bundle. `text=auto` leaves any binary alone. Laid down by ktl-sidecar
# Step 1; inert on a host without git.
* text=auto eol=lf
